{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of Adah and Zillah:</b> Do not set your heart to listen to the words of the Gaon [Saadia] in Exodus, for if we were to know the entire holy language, how would we be able to know all occurrences, like the meaning of Moses, Issachar,"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The Hebrew ends abruptly with 'Moses, Issachar,' apparently referring to personal names whose meanings are not determinable from language alone; rendered hyper-literally as the sentence stands without completion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:12.823616266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}